<title>USA: Uruguay buys 1 mln bbls Iranian light for June.</title>
<headline>Uruguay buys 1 mln bbls Iranian light for June.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uruguay's state oil refiner ANCAP bought one million barrels of Iranian light crude oil from Brazil's state oil company Petrobras in its latest crude tender, trade sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The crude will be delivered to Uruguay's Jose Ignacio terminal in the second half of June.</p>
<p>The price of the transaction was not disclosed, but the level was related to dated Brent, the sources said.</p>
<p>Iran Light crude has an API gravity of 33.1 degrees and a sulfur content of 1.5 percent.</p>
<p>((--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
